<title>RUSSIA: Russia copper, alloy exports double in July - agency.</title>
<headline>Russia copper, alloy exports double in July - agency.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian copper and copper alloy exports in July were 55,830 tonnes, double month-ago levels, Interfax news agency quoted the State Customs Committee as saying on Friday.</p>
<p>July refined copper exports were 53,270 tonnes of the total, it said. It gave no comparison figures.</p>
<p>The Netherlands imported 52,100 tonnes of Russia's copper and copper alloy shipments in July.</p>
<p>Copper and copper alloy exports for the first seven months of 1996 were 297,930 tonnes against 244,850 during the same period a year earlier, an increase of 21.7 percent, it said.</p>
<p>The data did not include trade with Belarus.</p>
<p>--Peter Henderson, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
